   <text:p text:style-name="P439"><text:bookmark-start text:name="__DdeLink__124882_552362995"/>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure3" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">4</text:sequence>: <text:span text:style-name="T716">Raw Property Write to 16-bit Property</text:span><text:bookmark-end text:name="__DdeLink__124882_552362995"/></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="Body">The following diagram <text:span text:style-name="T716">shows </text:span>an example of reading the value from <text:span text:style-name="Code">prop1</text:span>, which is assumed to be driven to <text:span text:style-name="Code">0x1111</text:span> by the worker. In this case, the worker asserts <text:span text:style-name="Code">data</text:span> and <text:span text:style-name="Code">done</text:span> one cycle after the read request appears on the interface.</text:p>
